        "description": "<p>Hi I\u2019m Chris, one of the co-founders of Shimmer (<a href=\"https://www.shimmer.care\">https://www.shimmer.care</a>), and today we\u2019re launching our new app called Indy (<a href=\"https://www.shimmer.care/indy\">https://www.shimmer.care/indy</a>). Indy is an ADHD app for structured planning, reflection, and self-awareness exercises. \nHere\u2019s a demo: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zDSDxyXv6i4\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zDSDxyXv6i4</a>.<p>We started Shimmer in 2022 after my adult ADHD diagnosis, and have shipped several iterations of ADHD support since then (1:1 coaching, web tools, body doubling, and AI-assisted coaching).<p>Across these launches and 80k coaching sessions, we kept running into the same constraint: \u201cknowing what to do\u201d is rarely the problem for people with ADHD. The harder problem is actually doing it consistently over time, especially when attention, motivation, and emotional state fluctuate.<p>That maps to a useful distinction that is explor",
